{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-161555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/dcc7c78752700a17970da69c3809a8c621aaf23580ab0c3329335083858bd019.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type II region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a type II region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $yz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type II region enclosed between the back surface $x={u}_{1}(y,z)=1$ and the front surface $x={u}_{2}(y,z)=3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/339d4658909da42d55a836af93c7fda425bbe8d0ce17f246b73a4ca28cb9f380.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le x\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $yz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9\\,⟺\\,z=\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/879425adc3b1e78a7ea6a59740c9d8634ac13f62dea8eedc764bb5f1b07c92c2.png)\n\nHence, $D={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}2y[x]_{x=1}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}4y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01d47be59c90936ecc9cd9b9b86b3d5832d12a7b862a48bd0f18389e526de556"} {"question" "q-161555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}4y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}8{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}4y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{4}xyz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{4}xyz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}yz{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x={z}^{2}}^{x=4}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}yz(\\frac{16}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{4}}{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}8yz-\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{5}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}8yz-\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{5}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}8yz-\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{5}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}4y[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=2}-\\frac{y}{12}[{z}^{6}]_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}4y(4-0)-\\frac{y}{12}(64-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}16y-\\frac{16}{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{32}{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}{[{y}^{2}]}_{y=-1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}(4-1) \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01d47be59c90936ecc9cd9b9b86b3d5832d12a7b862a48bd0f18389e526de556"} {"question" "q-161569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{z}(y+z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le z\\le 3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{z}(y+z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}(y+z)[x]_{x=y}^{x=z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+z)(z-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{3}{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}-{y}^{2}z]}_{z=y}^{z=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}(27-{y}^{3})-{y}^{2}(3-y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}9-\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}9-3{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[9y-{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =9-1+\\frac{1}{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01d47be59c90936ecc9cd9b9b86b3d5832d12a7b862a48bd0f18389e526de556"} {"question" "q-161573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "26"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{49}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{49}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}18x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le yz}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}18x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{yz}18x\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{yz}18x\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}18x\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[9{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=yz}dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}9(yz)^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}9{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}9{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}9{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[3{y}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,dy & =[{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01d47be59c90936ecc9cd9b9b86b3d5832d12a7b862a48bd0f18389e526de556"} {"question" "q-161579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{10}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/d148f8e38e2ad3bc7b1ca97a15b69c23ce315bc67ac2738009ca12f0fd7aef72.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/ead71a275dfa4d4a0e07a02400e30f85440b3af8ca5a7f8d0cf0ebed60da8a6a.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-2y+3z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/6e48e66eb003be316573e5b44948fcbce43b07e78fea97a7865ecf5eb4b4404a.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-2y+3z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-2y+3z}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-2y+3z}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-2y+3z}\\frac{yz}{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{yz}{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=4-2y+3z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{yz}{2}(4-2y+3z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(4yz-2{y}^{2}z+3y{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(4yz-2{y}^{2}z+3y{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(4yz-2{y}^{2}z+3y{z}^{2})\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{[2y{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(18y-9{y}^{2}+27y)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(45y-9{y}^{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(45y-9{y}^{2})\\,dy & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{45}{2}{y}^{2}-3{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(90-24)-0 \\\\  & =33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "01d47be59c90936ecc9cd9b9b86b3d5832d12a7b862a48bd0f18389e526de556"} {"question" "q-161782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "28"] ["math" "33"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "45"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"} {"question" "q-161782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "33"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/state.json" "file_sha256" "b08a1236f0538d4eb6daeffe072e30d31ad338f9c7738ca49b8b995b2ebed572"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2524 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
